\f1\b \
How to build
\f0\b0 \
\
\'95 Install the FreePascal 3.2.2 bootstrap compiler from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.freepascal.org/down/i386/macosx-hungary.html"}}{\fldrslt https://www.freepascal.org/down/i386/macosx-hungary.html}}\
\'95 Install the source code from above FPCSource commit.\
\'95 Patch the source code with the patches in the diffs folder\
\'95 Copy the build scripts into the folder where the sources are\
\'95 Double-click on a script in the Finder to run it.\
\'95 Run the unicodertl and llvm build scripts after the fpc build scripts.\
\
Please note that building the fpc-llvm compilers requires a fresh source code folder, \ul without\ulnone  the exceptvars-331.diff applied.\
\
\

\f1\b Where is fpc ?
\f0\b0 \
\
This compiler package includes four different compilers\
\
	{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "file:///usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1/ppca64"}}{\fldrslt /usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1/ppca64}} for arm64 fpc code\
	{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "file:///usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1/ppcx64"}}{\fldrslt /usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1/ppcx64}} for x86_64 fpc code\
	{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "file:///usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1-llvm/ppca64"}}{\fldrslt /usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1-llvm/ppca64}} for arm64 llvm code\
	{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "file:///usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1-llvm/ppca64"}}{\fldrslt /usr/local/lib/fpc/3.3.1-llvm/ppcx64}} for x86_64 llvm code\

\f1\b \
\
What\'92s new
\f0\b0 \
\
\'95 Changes for fpc-3.2.2 are given here {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wiki.freepascal.org/FPC_New_Features_3.2.2"}}{\fldrslt https://wiki.freepascal.org/FPC_New_Features_3.2.2}}\
\'95 Changes for fpc-3.2.4 are given here {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wiki.freepascal.org/User_Changes_3.2.4"}}{\fldrslt https://wiki.freepascal.org/User_Changes_3.2.4}}\
\'95 Changes for fpc-3.3.1 are given here {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wiki.freepascal.org/User_Changes_Trunk"}}{\fldrslt https://wiki.freepascal.org/User_Changes_Trunk}} and in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wiki.freepascal.org/FPC_New_Features_Trunk"}}{\fldrslt https://wiki.freepascal.org/FPC_New_Features_Trunk}}\
\
\'95 The compiler has been built with an additional "Unicode" runtime-library, see {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wiki.lazarus.freepascal.org/FPC_Unicode_RTL"}}{\fldrslt https://wiki.lazarus.freepascal.org/FPC_Unicode_RTL}}, but not with dotted namespace support. To use the "Unicode" runtime-library instead of the standard runtime-library, pass\
\
 	-tunicodertl\
\
to fpc. This may require source code changes. To check for building with the "Unicode" runtime-library, test the compiler define\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 	\{$ifdef UNICODERTL\}\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
The nonsensical name "Unicode" for UTF-16-treated-as-it-were-UCS-2 was invented by Microsoft and then for incomprehensible "compatibility" reasons copied by Delphi and FreePascal. The standard FPC runtime-library uses UTF-8, which is a lot more intelligent encoding.\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \
LLVM
\f0\b0 \
\
Included are compilers with LLVM {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://llvm.org/"}}{\fldrslt https://llvm.org}} code generation for aarch64 and x86_64, including their "Unicode" runtime-libraries. LLVM can do aggressive whole-program optimisation. In a few tests I did, it produced 20 to 30 % faster code. For best optimisation, pass\
\
	-O4 -Si -Clflto\
\
This enables optimisation level 4 (-O4), inlining (-Si) and whole-program-optimisation (-Clflto) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interprocedural_optimization"}}{\fldrslt https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interprocedural_optimization}}. You 
\f1\b must
\f0\b0  also pass\
\
	-Clvxx.x\
\
where xx.x is the clang version installed on your system. You can find out the version of clang by typing\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \CocoaLigature0 	clang --version\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \CocoaLigature1 in /Applications/Utilites/Terminal.app. It will respond with something like\
\
\pard\tx560\tx1120\tx1680\tx2240\tx2800\tx3360\tx3920\tx4480\tx5040\tx5600\tx6160\tx6720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \CocoaLigature0 	Apple clang version 15.0.0 (clang-1500.3.9.4)\
	Target: arm64-apple-darwin23.6.0\
	Thread model: posix\
	InstalledDir: /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/Toolchains/XcodeDefault.xctoolchain/usr/bin\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \CocoaLigature1 \
which implies that the version is 15.0 and the option to pass to fpc is\
\
	-Clv15.0\
\
The reason for this is that different versions of clang require different assembly code to be produced by fpc. If you emit this option, you will get various error messages from clang.\
\
In conditional code, you can check the\
\
	CPULLVM\
\
define, exported by the fpc llvm compiler.\
\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Using Address Sanitizer (asan)
\f0\b0 \
\
Address sanitizer is an LLVM code generation pass that instruments all memory accesses to provide (relatively) fast detection of reading uninitialised memory, buffer overruns, and accessing freed memory. It is similar to Valgrind, but faster, and also more accurate because LLVM knows exactly where each local and global variable starts and ends, so it can detect a pointer to one local/global variable crossing into the memory of another local/global variable.\
To use it, compile all units and the main program/library with \
\
	-Clfsanitize=address\
\
Some versions of address sanitizer automatically enable memory leak detection and abort the program if memory leaks are detected. You can disable this using\
\
	export ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=0\
\
See {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wiki.freepascal.org/LLVM"}}{\fldrslt https://wiki.freepascal.org/LLVM}}. Note that Address Sanitizer is also built into Xcode as a run-option of the executable.\
\
\

\f1\b Improved exception handling
\f0\b0 \
\
The patched fpc-3.2.4rc1 and 3.3.1 compilers add a compiler built-in define fpc_externalexceptvars and a compiler switch \cf3 \cb4 $externalexceptvars. \cf0 \cb1 The built-in define indicates whether the compiler switch is available, so that source code like this can still be compiled (but ignored) by other fpc compilers.\
\
\pard\tx346\pardeftab346\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \cb4 \{$ifdef fpc_externalexceptvars\}\
\{$externalexceptvars+\}\
\{$link /usr/local/lib/libexceptvars-1.0.dylib\}\
\{$endif\}\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \cb1 \
The compiler switch is available also as command-line switch  \cf2 \CocoaLigature0 -XLE.\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \ul \ulc0 \CocoaLigature1 Important\ulnone .\
Above code implies that \cf3 \cb4 /usr/local/lib/libexceptvars-1.0.dylib\cf0 \cb1  must be installed on user machines.\
\
The improved exception handling works by moving some internal variables from freepascal runtime libraries to \cf3 \cb4 libexceptvars-1.0.dylib\cf0 \cb1 . The problem with variables in the freepascal runtime libraries is that they are copied as static code into every binary compiled with freepascal, so that multiple instances of them exist. On the contrary, the exception handling variables in \cf3 \cb4 libexceptvars-1.0.dylib\cf0 \cb1  exist only once.\
\
This is not yet available for the llvm compiler.\
\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Asynchronous assembly
\f0\b0 \

\f1\b \
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 An option was added to execute the assembler phase asynchronously (out-of-process)\
\
